        "question": {
          ":question/id": "03079f99-0aaf-539e-a9de-56fac5bcf2c6",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\nx=5\\cos\\theta+1,\\quad y=7\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Isolate the trigonometric term in the $x$ equation, then square.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=5\\cos\\theta+1\\\\x-1&=5\\cos\\theta\\\\\\frac{x-1}{5}&=\\cos\\theta\\\\\\left(\\frac{x-1}{5}\\right)^2&=\\cos^2\\theta\\\\\\frac{(x-1)^2}{25}&=\\cos^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolate the trigonometric term in the $y$ equation, then square.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=7\\sin\\theta\\\\\\frac{y}{7}&=\\sin\\theta\\\\\\left(\\frac{y}{7}\\right)^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\frac{y^2}{49}&=\\sin^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the squared equations and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{49}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nThus the Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{49}=1.\n$$\n\nThe full parameter interval traces the entire ellipse.",
