          ":question/id": "0206d34d-9063-53df-9153-1a1a1cd6a010",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4}{5}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{4}{3}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Isolate the trigonometric term in the $x$ equation, then square.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=\\frac{4}{5}\\cos\\theta\\\\\\frac{5}{4}x&=\\cos\\theta\\\\\\left(\\frac{5}{4}x\\right)^2&=\\cos^2\\theta\\\\\\frac{25}{16}x^2&=\\cos^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIsolate the trigonometric term in the $y$ equation, then square.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=\\frac{4}{3}\\sin\\theta\\\\\\frac{y}{\\frac{4}{3}}&=\\sin\\theta\\\\\\left(\\frac{y}{\\frac{4}{3}}\\right)^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\frac{9}{16}y^2&=\\sin^2\\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the squared equations and use $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{16}x^2+\\frac{9}{16}y^2=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nThus the Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{16}x^2+\\frac{9}{16}y^2=1.\n$$\n\nThe full parameter interval traces the entire ellipse.",
